From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Alexandre Derumier <aderumier@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 07:40:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] winedmo: Fall back to system memory samples when the D3D
 sample allocation fails.

The video decoder is D3D11 aware: given a DXGI device manager, its
sample allocator makes D3D11 textures of the output type. The MPEG-4
Part 2 decoder's first output type is YUY2 (as Windows' decoder), and
DXVK cannot create DXGI_FORMAT_YUY2 textures ("D3D11: Cannot create
texture: Format 107"): InitializeSampleAllocatorEx() fails with
E_INVALIDARG, every ProcessOutput() fails and the source reader stops
the stream ("Failed to initialize allocator, hr 0x80070057").

When the D3D allocation fails, drop the device manager from the
allocator and output system memory samples, as without a D3D manager;
the video processor the source reader inserts after the decoder takes
them and converts on the device.

Game impacted: Big Foot Crush (UNIS, Unity 2022): its attract movie
(mp4v 1280x720, played by Unity's VideoPlayer through the source reader
in ARGB32) never showed, "WindowsVideoMedia error 0x80070057 ...
IMFSourceReader::WaitForSample". Plays with the patch (RADV, DXVK).
---
--- a/dlls/winedmo/video_decoder.c
+++ b/dlls/winedmo/video_decoder.c
@@ -721,7 +721,16 @@
 
     if (FAILED(hr = IMFVideoSampleAllocatorEx_InitializeSampleAllocatorEx(decoder->allocator, 10, 10,
             decoder->attributes, decoder->output_type)))
-        return hr;
+    {
+        /* The D3D device may not create textures of the output format (YUY2 with DXVK):
+         * output system memory samples instead, as a decoder without a D3D manager. */
+        WARN("Failed to allocate D3D samples, hr %#lx, using system memory samples.\n", hr);
+        if (FAILED(hr = IMFVideoSampleAllocatorEx_SetDirectXManager(decoder->allocator, NULL)))
+            return hr;
+        if (FAILED(hr = IMFVideoSampleAllocatorEx_InitializeSampleAllocatorEx(decoder->allocator, 10, 10,
+                decoder->attributes, decoder->output_type)))
+            return hr;
+    }
     decoder->allocator_initialized = TRUE;
     return S_OK;
 }
